1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,300
Ryo-san, Christmas is almost here.

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:10,380
Christmas, my foot. Everyone's
just canoodling all over the place.

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:13,486
Christmas is basically Christ's birthday,

4
00:00:13,536 --> 00:00:15,520
it's not a day for couples, you know.

5
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,760
Ryo-san, you're always alone, aren't you?

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,060
Shut up.

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,320
Damn it. Give me a present too.

8
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:31,140
When you watch TV, keep the room
bright and sit back a bit, will you?

9
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:44,280
Those without money, come to me.

10
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:49,060
I've got none either, but don't you worry.

11
00:00:49,060 --> 00:01:02,980
Look, blue skies, white clouds,
somehow it'll all work out.

12
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:19,900
Those without jobs, come to me.

13
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:24,540
I've got none either, so don't worry.

14
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:31,560
Look, the steel clouds are burning.

15
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:38,280
Somehow it'll all work out.

16
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,540
You understand, right? Right, right.

17
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:47,380
Once you understand,
keep quiet and follow me.

18
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,280
Fly! Shoulder Counter!

19
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:09,620
No good, no good!

20
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,040
Damn it!

21
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,120
Alright, this time it's good!

22
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:16,980
I'm such a genius!

23
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,380
Ugh, the racket in broad daylight.

24
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,520
Senpai, what are you doing?

25
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:23,940
Well, I'm not sure what it is, but

26
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:26,420
Of course it's you.
You were putting something together.

27
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,120
Is he building a life-size
model kit or something?

28
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,560
It suddenly got quiet, didn't it?

29
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,100
Let's go take a look.

30
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:34,500
Yeah.

31
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,700
Senpai, what is that?

32
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:56,660
Can't you tell by looking?

33
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,480
It's a one-person helicopter.

34
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,680
A helicopter?

35
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:03,400
That's right,
an auto-gyro made even more compact.

36
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:07,380
A shoulder copter. It's basically a
bamboo copter with a motor attached.

37
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,540
I call it the Bamboo Copter.

38
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:12,820
Hey, I've heard that name somewhere before.

39
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:15,840
Then I'll call it the Shoulder Copter.

40
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:19,760
That's pretty simple.
But will it really let you fly?

41
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,640
If it doesn't fly,
it's just a big electric fan, right?

42
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:26,700
But with that shape,
won't it spin the person wearing it too?

43
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,660
Don't worry. The shaft and body
have multiple layers of gears,

44
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:34,480
so they sync in the opposite
direction to the propeller's rotation.

45
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:38,400
No matter the rotation speed,
the front always stays fixed.

46
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:40,720
That's groundbreaking.

47
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,540
Just hearing about it, it sounds amazing.

48
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:45,680
This is the first prototype.

49
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:48,840
If this succeeds,
we'll put it on the market in a big way.

50
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,660
You're going to sell it?

51
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,060
Of course.

52
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:55,320
Do you think I'd build something
like this just as a hobby?

53
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,960
Modern business is a fight over every minute and second,
you know.

54
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:04,400
Even when the cars won't move an inch.

55
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,080
Even though we have cell phones and email,

56
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:11,320
there are still times you have to
meet face-to-face and talk directly.

57
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:13,520
There's no time.

58
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,060
That's exactly when

59
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:19,980
it shines!

60
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:32,400
Well, everyone, sorry to keep you waiting.

61
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,540
That's how it works.

62
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,720
The first unit was handmade
and cost over a million yen,

63
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:41,540
but with a sponsor and mass production,
we can sell it for half the price.

64
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:45,520
Before long, this Shoulder Copter will
be flitting about like a red dragonfly,

65
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:49,200
soaring through the city sky at sunset.
That day is sure to come!

66
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:51,160
That's a kind of creepy sight, isn't it?

67
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,420
Even delivery services for
high-rise apartment buildings

68
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,660
will soon stop using elevators

69
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,360
and start relying on this thing.

70
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:01,760
Put that way,
there might be quite a wide demand for it.

71
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,960
Do you think so?

72
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,060
Of course it is!

73
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:05,780
Alright, let's give it a try.

74
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,360
I can't open it.

75
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:12,040
It's impossible inside the room, after all.

76
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,720
Alright, let's go to the park.

77
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,760
We should have just done
it here from the start

78
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,660
Here we go.

79
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,400
It looks pretty heavy.

80
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,520
It weighs 30 kilos, you know.

81
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,860
Well, it has an engine,
so there's no help for it.

82
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:30,000
Are you all right? Don't get lost, okay?

83
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,280
Yeah, if anything happens,
I'll contact you on my cell phone.

84
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,160
Understood.

85
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:37,320
Then stand back, you two. It's dangerous.

86
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:39,120
I'm starting the engine.

87
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:39,760
Yes.

88
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,880
Engine start!

89
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,840
Taking off!

90
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,140
It's up

91
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,520
It worked, senpai!

92
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:58,480
Later! I'm going to do a
test flight around Tokyo.

93
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:01,180
If the Chief shows up, cover for me!

94
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:02,680
He's gone.

95
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:04,960
It really does look like a dragonfly.

96
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:12,500
Alright, going smoothly, going smoothly!

97
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,440
Whee!

98
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,540
What a great view.

99
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:23,980
Maybe I really am a genius after all.

100
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,780
Now, I wonder how things look down below.

101
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:34,360
Found the temple family!

102
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,720
Alright, let's mess with them a little.

103
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,820
Wow, that looks fun!

104
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,220
Yeah! Let's ride! Let's ride!

105
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:47,880
It's high.
I'm not good with this kind of thing.

106
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,600
It's fine, Daddy!

107
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:50,720
This is the best!

108
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,160
As long as you keep your eyes closed,
you'll be fine.

109
00:06:55,210 --> 00:06:57,940
It's not like we're really
flying through the sky.

110
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:10,640
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

111
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,380
Making all this racket
over such a trifling thing!

112
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:16,420
Alright, let's give them a
proper aerial sightseeing tour.

113
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:17,680
Here we go!

114
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,200
Whoooa!

115
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,020
Whoooa!

116
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,380
Hehehe

117
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,160
Terai's gonna be shocked!

118
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,380
Whoa!

119
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:26,900
Whoa!

120
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,180
Here I go!

121
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:29,280
Whoa!

122
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,700
Mama!

123
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,140
Whoa!

124
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:32,600
Whoa!

125
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,820
It's like we're flying through the sky!

126
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,420
Rapid ascent!

127
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,620
Whoa!

128
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,360
Steep dive!

129
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,180
A figure-eight flight!

130
00:07:44,320 --> 00:08:14,280


131
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,700
Whoaaaaaaaa!

132
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,440
That was way too thrilling!

133
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,720
That was close

134
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,300
Hello, it's me.

135
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,640
Senpai, how's the test flight going?

136
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:30,600
Going smoothly, smoothly.

137
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,520
Please be careful!

138
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:35,120
I hope he's all right,
Ryo-chan really is something.

139
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:40,460
They're playing baseball!

140
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:42,140
Ugh!

141
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,680
Hahaha!

142
00:08:48,920 --> 00:09:02,200


143
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,440
Not wanted here.

144
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,940
Not wanted here

145
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,780
My apologies.

146
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,280
Goodbye.

147
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,820
I don't get it.

148
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,380
That was a terrible experience.

149
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,540
Out of gas

150
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:30,220
I should refuel soon.

151
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:32,780
Whoa!

152
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,000
Whoa!

153
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:39,680
A gas station!

154
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:41,480
Fill 'er up!

155
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,360
W-why from the sky?

156
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:46,360
High-octane, fill it up!

157
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,140
Yes! Welcome!

158
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,400
Yes, okay.

159
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:56,620
Now, back to it. Move, move!

160
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,200
One, two, pillow!

161
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,120
What was that just now?

162
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,700
You there, young sports car! Stop!

163
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,500
Stop, damn you!

164
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:14,420
It's me.

165
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,760
You're 30 kilometers over the speed limit.

166
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,380
Yoohoo, Honda!

167
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,960
What's that, fisherman?

168
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,640
Let me take a break.

169
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,980
Hey, Mariroy is on the job.

170
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:33,340
It's fine, it's fine,
don't be so stiff about it.

171
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,720
So say "please get off," then!

172
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:45,100
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

173
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,240
I'm scared!

174
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,120
Hey, don't struggle!

175
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:56,100
This happened because you
suddenly raised the output valve!

176
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,000
Please don't bring me down so fast.

177
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:03,600
Stop thrashing around!
It's hard to control with one hand!

178
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:05,720
Scared, Ryo-chan!

179
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,680
Engine trouble!

180
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,980
Aaaaaah!

181
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,000
Aaaaaah!

182
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Aaaaaah!

183
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:16,620
Eek!

184
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:17,380
Mm?

185
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,920
What?

186
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,800
Engine, hang in there!

187
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,760
The engine's back!

188
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,740
Bail out!

189
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,180
My hip's coming off!

190
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:31,860
Let go!

191
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:38,000
Senpai, the family's clinging to us!

192
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,100
This guy's insane, let go!

193
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:42,960
My waist is tearing off!

194
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,760
Forgive us!

195
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:04,680
Well, so

196
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:08,940
Gas and maintenance cost
more than I expected.

197
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:13,060
We have to get this into production no matter what,
or we'll be in huge debt!

198
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:15,160
And now for the next news.

199
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:19,360
Known as the pet of King Ahosutan,
who is visiting Japan as a state guest,

200
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:21,920
the top-performing Chappy has gone missing.

201
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:25,180
Chappy boasts an IQ of 380,

202
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,300
a bird that can speak human language,

203
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:30,460
a bird so famous that its name is even
recorded in the New Historical Records.

204
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:33,480
King Ahosutan is said to be deeply shocked.

205
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:36,940
There are also rumors that anti-king
factions kidnapped it, but...

206
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:42,740
They're offering a reward of 100 million
Ahosutan dollars to whoever finds it.

207
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:43,200
That's it!

208
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,980
If we catch it using the Shoulder Copter,

209
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:49,800
we'll get the reward and great publicity!

210
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,240
We'll even get sponsors!

211
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:55,400
Hey!

212
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,880
Chappy! Hey!

213
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,600
Come out!

214
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,880
Where are you?!

215
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,500
Excuse me, have you seen this bird?

216
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:10,780
I-I-I may have!

217
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,140
Did you see this bird around here?

218
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,780
Excuse me, but did a bird like this fly by?

219
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:48,180
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

220
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:50,340
Hold on, we're at the top of a chimney!

221
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,440
Dekkochō!

222
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:55,260
There you are! You're Chappy, aren't you!

223
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,320
Ferry

224
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,192
This d -

225
00:13:57,242 --> 00:14:25,840
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeek!

226
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:32,540
There it is!

227
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,520
Full throttle!

228
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:34,800
Nyagaah!

229
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:36,300
Damn you!

230
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,140
Whirr! Whirr!

231
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,320
Wobble! Wobble!

232
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,180
Whoa! The world's turned pink!

233
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,280
W-what is this?

234
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:43,700
Thief! Underwear thief!

235
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,340
Eek! It's the underwear thief!

236
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,960
W-w-wait! I'm -

237
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,160
You're the underwear thief!

238
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,060
Thief! Underwear thief!

239
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:52,300
Underwear thief!

240
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,760
So it's you!

241
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:56,320
The underwear thief who's
been terrorizing this area!

242
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:57,600
It's a misunderstanding!

243
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,660
I'm in the same line of work!

244
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,160
Damn! Time to beat a retreat!

245
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,220
Hahahaha! I'm on a roll!

246
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,400
What an outrageous bird!
Where the hell did it go?

247
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:09,700
Ah, I'm on a roll!

248
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:13,960
He's up there!

249
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:14,580
Yeah, yeah!

250
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,540
Alright, here goes!

251
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,380
Whoa!

252
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:19,240
I'm gonna crash right into the king!

253
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,480
What the hell is this thing!

254
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:24,400
Hahaha! Tōho! Tōho!

255
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:25,500
What are you doing!

256
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,920
Whoa! Ryotsu!

257
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:29,720
You there, what do you think you're
doing up in a place like that!

258
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:33,900
With me in this great form, this prize money

259
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:37,700
What are you babbling about, Saborio?
Come down here!

260
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:41,000
Chief, you idiot! You idiot!

261
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:41,900
What did you say?

262
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,940
H-hey, what are you doing?!

263
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:46,440
Your feet stink, how creepy!

264
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,660
No, stop it! Hey, wait a second!

265
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:51,120
Ryotsu, you've got some nerve!

266
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:55,120
No, no, Chief, I didn't say that.
It was this guy here!

267
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:59,260
Enough with the lies!
A bird can't talk, you know!

268
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,820
No, it's true, I swear!

269
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:02,080
Say something!

270
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:03,600
Peechiko, paachiko

271
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,540
Hey, don't play dumb with me!

272
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:07,820
You're the one playing dumb!

273
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:09,340
Get down here, Gyotz!

274
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:12,660
No way! Come and get me, nyah-nyah-nyah!

275
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:13,740
Hey, you! Get back here!

276
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,440
Gyotz! You idiot!

277
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:19,600
Don't think you'll get away with this!
You're writing a report for this!

278
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:21,980
I told you, it wasn't me!

279
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:26,040
Damn it! He says whatever he wants and runs off!
I'm not letting him get away with this!

280
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,160
There it is!

281
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:44,780
Right, operation start!
We're going to kidnap King Ahosutan.

282
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:48,560
What?

283
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,480
What are you doing? Talk! Spill it!

284
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:00,160
This is bad! The king -

285
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,520
Where the hell did he go?

286
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:13,760
Whenever you actually look for him,
he's nowhere to be found.

287
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,500
Ryotsu, Ryotsu.

288
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:17,500
There you are.

289
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,360
Ryotsu, don't slack off!

290
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,400
Yeah, shut up.

291
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,180
It makes me angry,
it's like the real Chief is scolding me.

292
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,380
Ryotsu, this way, this way!

293
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:27,800
Damn it, wait!

294
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,940
You

295
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:36,140
What do you think you're gonna do with me

296
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,040
It's this way, right!

297
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:43,200
Hurry up, Hotary!

298
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:44,400
Shut up!

299
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:46,020
Take care of him, you!

300
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:51,500
Let him talk all he wants, full throttle!

301
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,840
This time I'll catch you for sure!

302
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:54,940
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

303
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,340
This way! This way!

304
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,540
There, I did it!

305
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:03,020
I can grill you into yakitori and eat you,
or do whatever I please.

306
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,800
Bee! Trouble! Big trouble, nyaa!

307
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:09,530
What's the trouble?
Now you're scared for your life

308
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,380
but I'm not forgiving you, you know.

309
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:15,480
Bee! Bee! King kidnapped!
Ana-heli! Ana-heli, yaah!

310
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:18,951
King kidnapped?
What nonsense are you babbling about,

311
00:18:19,001 --> 00:18:20,380
you liar?

312
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,600
It's true! It's true! I'm not lying!

313
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:26,420
Even if you try to cover it up with that,
I'm not falling for it!

314
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,020
It's true! It's true! Slurp!

315
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:31,600
Damn it! Get back here!

316
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:33,520
Tereee! Pee!

317
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:34,500
Wait!

318
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:37,440
Pee! Hurry up, you're too slow!

319
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:40,240
Hey! You! Crap! Get inside!

320
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:41,860
I'm going this way! Damn it!

321
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:43,420
Whoa! So dangerous!

322
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,780
Damn it! Annoying snake!

323
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,480
Ryotsu! Keria! Inside the keri!

324
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:53,180
That's King Ahosutan!

325
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:56,240
So your story was true?

326
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,760
Ryotsu, please, take care of this, please!

327
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:04,680
Alright, but in return, you'd better cooperate
properly so I get the reward, understand?

328
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:05,520
Got it.

329
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,140
Alright, let's go!

330
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:13,820
Once we're out at sea, the submarine's waiting.
The operation's a complete success!

331
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:18,160
Ryo-san, a strange helicopter has
been hovering around for a while now.

332
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:18,800
What?

333
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:23,880
That's Chappy!
Here, it's here, it's right here!

334
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:24,760
Heave!

335
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,040
Got it! Leave it to me!

336
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:33,200
Whoa! Take this!

337
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:36,180
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

338
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:44,600
Hey! At this rate we can't get close without being reckless!
Fall back for now!

339
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:52,835
Alright! If it's come to this, I'll draw the machine gun fire!
You charge into Hell,

340
00:19:52,885 --> 00:19:53,980
untie the king's ropes!

341
00:19:55,780 --> 00:20:00,580
We'll make it work!
Here we go, here we go! This way, this way!

342
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,660
Now, Chappy!

343
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,200
Krillin!

344
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,360
Zephyrshah!

345
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,900
Chappy!

346
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,560
Hey! What are you doing! This way, this way!

347
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,100
Fly up!

348
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,220
Running away?

349
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:55,160
Feeling great, feeling great!

350
00:20:56,500 --> 00:21:00,920
Well done, Chappy, you really pulled it off.

351
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:04,320
Pipi, Ryotsu is amazing, Ryotsu is amazing!

352
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:06,860
Good, good, you get it, don't you?

353
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:21,140
Mr. Ryotsu, you found Chappy, didn't you?

354
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:23,220
As a thank-you, I'm awarding you a prize.

355
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,720
Congratulations, congratulations.

356
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:29,600
It worked out!
The 100 million Ahostandalers are ours.

357
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,760
My future is rosy.

358
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:36,320
Alright, Mr. Ryotsu,
100 million Ahostandalers!

359
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,940
So this is 100 million Aho-Standalers?

360
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:49,040
By the way, how much is 100
million Aho-Standalers in yen?

361
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:51,680
At today's rate, it's about 5,780.

362
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:55,120
5,780 yen? Well, that's not bad.

363
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:58,220
That's 5,780 yen, sir.

364
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,860
No way! After all that hard work!

365
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,480
Even if you prepare for it...

366
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:10,980
Today, 1 yen is about
17,301 Aho-Standalers, so...

367
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:15,960
So 100 million Aho-Standalers
is about 5,780 yen?

368
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,060
Well, why didn't you say so sooner!

369
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:21,160
Ryotsu, too bad! Too bad!

370
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:24,640
Hey, you bastard, this isn't over!

371
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:26,660
Funny, funny!

372
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:28,440
Even the people of this world...

373
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,100
Ryotsu, you good-for-nothing!

374
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,040
Enough already!

375
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:34,260
You damn fool Ryotsu, you good-for-nothing!

376
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,640
Shut up!

377
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:48,220
H-hey, what did you do! I can't control it!

378
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:51,060
Ryotsu-tsu, bye-bye, bye-bye, top form!

379
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:53,900
Thanks a lot, Mister Ryotsu!

380
00:22:59,700 --> 00:23:01,158
The King of Aho-Standal

381
00:23:01,208 --> 00:23:05,280
has set off for home with the heroic,
top-form Chappy.

382
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:07,136
An IQ of 380, you know,

383
00:23:07,186 --> 00:23:09,920
so it really wasn't just an ordinary bird.

384
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:15,320
Exactly. I'd like to make someone
drink a brew of his fingernail clippings.

385
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:17,800
Speaking of which,
I wonder what happened to Senpai.

386
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,760
We haven't seen his face in a while.

387
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,540
And now, news from overseas.

388
00:23:21,540 --> 00:23:25,360
At the summit of Mount McKinley,
the highest peak of the Alaska Range,

389
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,740
a creature resembling a
yeti has been discovered.

390
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:32,400
the creature makes strange cries, saying,
"I am Ryotsu!"

391
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,120
Ryo-chan.

392
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:36,980
Senpai, he was blown all the
way to Alaska by the jet stream.

393
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:39,760
He looks like a dandelion seed.

394
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:42,500
Perfect. Leave him be, leave him be.

395
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:45,840
It'd be better if he spent
his whole life as Alaska's yeti.

396
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:48,080
It'd be for the good of
the world and its people.

397
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,860
I'm Ryotsu!

398
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:58,700
Somebody help me!

399
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:01,240
Somebody help me!

400
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:20,240
Like someone calling out to
you after the rain has stopped,

401
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:27,080
I walked looking back,
led along by the gachapon machines.

402
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:34,260
That strange feeling I had back then.

403
00:24:34,260 --> 00:24:39,480
So on the arcade street's tiles,

404
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:45,260
I tried walking only on the black ones.

405
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

406
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:57,580
Politicians with their self-important faces,

407
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,860
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow, too.

408
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:06,480
Try turning at that corner over there.

409
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:11,940
You can meet everyone, everyone.

410
00:25:11,940 --> 00:25:19,640
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there's Kame-ari.

411
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,840
Everyone, come on over to our town!

412
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:26,420
Thank you.

413
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:33,000
A new invention, jumbo manju?

414
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:35,520
Eat it and you can have any build you want?

415
00:25:35,620 --> 00:25:37,900
Looking down on Nakagawa feels great!

416
00:25:38,040 --> 00:25:40,040
Hey, wait!
How big is this thing going to get?

417
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,580
This is way too big!

418
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:43,600
Do something! You crazy professor!

419
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:46,180
Next time: Ryo-san gets big!

420
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:47,120
See you next time!

421
00:26:00,860 --> 00:26:01,580
Start!

